<<music startambient>>
<<background firstmemory>>
Thepromeus: I once knew somebody.
Thepromeus: A girl, with a bright smile and determination that could bring the world down.
Thepromeus: The girl, lost in her own mind, had big dreams for the future.
Thepromeus: But unfortunately the future that holded her was a bleek one.
Thepromeus: Towering gigants were build, the greenery of the ground that once was had been replaced with metal and cooper.
Thepromeus: All that once was organic had been replaced by components.
Thepromeus: This girl. Decided to opose the gigants.
Thepromeus: She was a tall leader despite her age, she made the weak rally.
Thepromeus: She promised "We will bring the fire to them, so they may feel what we feel everyday of our existence"
Thepromeus: She didn't have a plan, well maybe one.
Thepromeus: To keep dreaming, and to spread hope to all.
Thepromeus: That they weren't alone, and that together they might take the world from the powers that be.
Thepromeus: Perhaps then, that's why they got rid of her.
Thepromeus: A shame, I liked the talkings off this little soul.
Thepromeus: Maybe it's cause we didn't think that those who were born in the metal age had this passion for the world that once was.
        ->You: You are talking about me, right?
<<sfx choice>>
Thepromeus: Dreams, that word. too big for your own good.
Thepromeus: Desires, Too unstable, too many variables for them.
Thepromeus: That's why they decided to put you in a little caccon.
Thepromeus: Like the rest of them.
Thepromeus: I pitty you. 
Thepromeus: At least you don't get to remember how we suffered.
Thepromeus: Farewell young one.
Thepromeus: Trust only your soul.
Thepromeus: Godspeed.
